      {
        "id": 40621,
        "name": "infusco",
        "username": "infusco",
        "avatar_template": "/letter_avatar_proxy/v4/letter/i/d2c977/{size}.png",
        "created_at": "2012-10-22T21:16:04.000Z",
        "cooked": "<p>Okay, now I'm confused because you stated affects every possible target.</p><p>So let me rephrase this:</p><p>Villain is playing against four heroes. All four heroes have 3 pieces of equipment, for a total of 12 pieces of equipment spread across the heroes.</p><p>Villain card says it destroys 2 pieces of (unspecified) target hero equipment. Which of these is accurate:</p><p>- 2 out of those 12 pieces gets destroyed, meaning two out of the four heroes lose 1 piece of equipment (2 pieces total)<br>- Each hero loses 2 pieces of equipment, for a total of 8 pieces out of the 12 on the table (2 pieces each).</p>",
        "post_number": 6,
        "post_type": 1,
        "updated_at": "2021-02-07T02:14:18.212Z",
        "reply_count": 0,
        "reply_to_post_number": null,
        "quote_count": 0,
