        "id": 40624,
        "name": "Cosmonaut Zero",
        "username": "Cosmonaut_Zero",
        "avatar_template": "/user_avatar/forums.greaterthangames.com/cosmonaut_zero/{size}/2520_2.png",
        "created_at": "2012-10-22T21:34:17.000Z",
        "cooked": "<p><span>\"<em>2 out of those 12 pieces gets destroyed, meaning two out of the four heroes lose 1 piece of equipment (2 pieces total)</em>\" is very nearly correct. If you wanted you could have one hero lose 2 pieces of equipment.</span></p><p><span>Generally the rule of interpretation is: do the thing the card says and only the thing the card says. There are a few addendums like \"any time you see 'would' add an 'instead,'\" and some stuff to sort out timing, but doing precisely the thing the card says - no more and no less - will get you 90% of the way there. In this case, if it meant for each hero to destroy 2 pieces of equipment it would read something like \"Each hero destroys 2 Equipment cards.\"</span></p>",
        "post_number": 8,
        "post_type": 1,
        "updated_at": "2021-02-07T02:14:18.366Z",
        "reply_count": 0,
        "reply_to_post_number": null,
