        "raw": "<p><span style=\"font-family: Helvetica, Arial, sans-serif; font-size: 14px; line-height: 23px; background-color: rgb(255, 255, 255); \">&quot;<em>2 out of those 12 pieces gets destroyed, meaning two out of the four heroes lose 1 piece of equipment (2 pieces total)</em>&quot; is very nearly correct. If you wanted you could have one hero lose 2 pieces of equipment.</span></p><p><span style=\"font-family: Helvetica, Arial, sans-serif; font-size: 14px; line-height: 23px; background-color: rgb(255, 255, 255); \">Generally the rule of interpretation is: do the thing the card says and only the thing the card says. There are a few addendums like &quot;any time you see &#39;would&#39; add an &#39;instead,&#39;&quot; and some stuff to sort out timing, but doing precisely the thing the card says - no more and no less - will get you 90% of the way there. In this case, if it meant for each hero to destroy 2 pieces of equipment it would read something like &quot;Each hero destroys 2 Equipment cards.&quot;</span></p>",
